## Destination Guide

Rishikesh is known for its spiritual ambiance and has been a popular destination for yogis and seekers. The region is also famous for its scenic beauty, cultural heritage, and various adventure activities.

## Best Time to Visit
- **Best Season:** The best time to visit Rishikesh is between October to February when the temperature ranges between 12°C - 30°C. The days are pleasant, and evenings can be chilly.
- **Peak Tourist Season:** Peak tourist season in Rishikesh starts from December through March.

## Top Attractions & Activities
- **Triveni Ghat** — Located on the banks of River Ganga, it is a significant spot for spiritual and religious purposes. (Source: [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i7tMHOQGsWo))
- **Laxman Jhula** — A suspension bridge that connects the old and new Rishikesh town. (Source: [Aeronfly Travel Consultants on Quora](https://aeronflytravelconsultants.quora.com/What-are-the-best-places-to-visit-in-Rishikesh-if-I-have-only-one-day))
- **Rajaji National Park** — Home to a variety of wildlife including tigers, leopards, and elephants (Source: [ makemytrip](https://www.makemytrip.com/tripideas/places/rishikesh))
- **Dhyan Ganesh Temple & Adi Guru Rudrlingeshwar Temple** — Known for its beautiful architecture and historical significance.
- **Lakshman Jhula** — Popular among tourists for its serene views and evening walk. (Source: [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i7tMHOQGsWo))
- **Har Ki Pauri** — Considered one of the most sacred spots in Rishikesh, associated with Lord Ram’s stay.

